# M3 identity manifest - 15 files.
#
# RULE: every hash below is defined over LF line endings.
#
# Why: the sealed M1/M2 working tree (%TEMP%\opencode\a066m2-f13-optimization\
# repo-m2) stores its .rs files with CRLF, because it was produced on Windows,
# while the commits they came from (C2 59e5de5f, base c83db1fc) store LF. The
# commit procedure therefore applies exactly one transformation, CRLF -> LF, and
# this manifest describes the result.
#
# The transformation is EOL-only and content preserving. Two proofs:
#   1. every file satisfies b.replace(b"\r\n", b"\n") == b.replace(b"\r", b""),
#      i.e. nothing but the line terminator changes;
#   2. after normalisation the three BX/BY/C0 files hash to the exact blobs of
#      base commit c83db1fc02db93d2a62a7e5e4ee80781f9488eb7:
#        2e3330872ad78760b9021bd1296b28ed66ef565e  tests/phase4bx_dag_topology_tests.rs
#        11c9de298bbb9d5861c99fdd355a460f3b803a2e  tests/phase4by_ledger_apply_benchmark_tests.rs
#        0eb2625076a82301cd86b868b8cd79ea8872bb46  tests/phase4c0_full_pipeline_benchmark_tests.rs
#      Normalisation restores the upstream bytes; it does not invent new ones.
#      Their SHA-256 is unchanged because those three files were already LF.
#
# A tree that does not match these values is NOT the M1+M2 tree.
#
